From 1c3f609fb205e317a4e3502327ccf97893770ab5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 15:06:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] llama : fail restoring a truncated sequence state file
 instead of aborting

llama_io_read_file inherited llama_file::read_raw()'s tolerance for reads
past the end of the file (it zero-fills, to allow for direct I/O alignment
padding). A truncated state file was therefore "read" successfully, nread
overran the file size and GGML_ASSERT(nread <= state_size) aborted the
process, e.g. when llama-server restored a half-written slot save.

Check the remaining file size in read() and read_tensor() and throw, which
llama_state_seq_load_file already turns into a failed restore. Also remove
the partially restored sequence if a restore throws part-way, and bound the
length fields of the server's checkpoint appendix by the remaining file size.

No change to the on-disk format.

